# Staging's secrets: copy to secrets.staging.env in the repo root
# (git-ignored), which every deploy uploads as secrets.env for the unit to
# load (docs/staging.md). An empty file boots on the public placeholders in
# config/staging.yaml; mail then fails to send.
#
# JWT_SECRET: staging's own, never production's: a staging token must not
# open a production account. Base64, as Loco decodes it before signing: a
# value that isn't (the placeholder "replace-me" is not) boots fine and then
# refuses every sign-in. Make one with `openssl rand -base64 48`.
# JWT_SECRET=

# Mail, only when staging should send real mail: all four together. Host on
# 587 with STARTTLS (465 needs MAILER_PORT=465 and `tls: implicit` in the
# config); an app password, never the account's; the sender as
# "Name <address>", in double quotes, on the account's address or domain
# (details in docs/production.md).
# MAILER_HOST=
# MAILER_USER=
# MAILER_PASSWORD=
# MAILER_FROM="App <noreply@stg.example.com>"
